# The dark band climbing the terrain, as a time series at the tw_east repro state.
#
# tw_east (harness_runs/20260925_211036_repro_night_terrain/captures/tw_east.png) is the frame in
# question: red-lit ridge, and a grey band on the ground below it whose upper edge traces UP the
# slope. This runs the same instant (Sun 0.96 deg below the horizon) with the same observer,
# camera and settings, then walks it forward in 5-minute steps so that edge can be compared with
# where the shadow line sits at each step.
#
# Anchor: sh_t00 was written to be pixel-identical to tw_east. It is not, and it should not be -
# the shader has changed under it, and the 92,969 differing pixels are the fix (see the result note
# below). Re-running this expecting the match means expecting the grey slab back.
#
# The `sunvis` captures are the shadow line itself: R = sunDiscVis (0 when the Sun's disc is below
# that point's own horizon), G = geoSunDot + dipSin (0 exactly ON the line, negative below it),
# B = dipSin at the point's altitude (sat_sky.frag:2454-2455, 2655). Comparing each beauty capture's
# light/dark edge to its sunvis G zero-crossing says whether that edge is the shadow line or a
# constant-altitude contour.
#
# Result (first run, 2026-09-25 23:03, harness_runs/shadow_trace): sh_t00 differs from tw_east.png in
# 92,969 pixels - the grey slab is gone - because `tDirectSun` is now multiplied by sunDiscVis
# (sat_sky.frag:2591-2596, the fix for "the grey slab of 2026-09-25"). The slab was the direct-sun
# term's 0.05 sunLit floor, 0.15 terrain-shadow floor and dayFrac soft gate leaking a NEUTRAL wash
# onto ground the Sun cannot reach - the same ground the eye reads as "Earth's shadow", which is why
# its edge tracked the terminator up the slope. It was never the shadow itself being non-black.
preset High
set clouds.coverage 0
set clouds.fog_coverage 0
observer lat=56.1 lon=-159.6 agl=450
camera az=90 el=3 fov=60
time set 2026-11-21T21:04:50Z
time pause
wait settle
capture sh_t00
debugview sunvis
wait settle
capture sh_t00_sunvis
debugview off

time add 300
wait settle
capture sh_t05
debugview sunvis
wait settle
capture sh_t05_sunvis
debugview off

time add 300
wait settle
capture sh_t10
debugview sunvis
wait settle
capture sh_t10_sunvis
debugview off

time add 300
wait settle
capture sh_t15
debugview sunvis
wait settle
capture sh_t15_sunvis
debugview off

time add 300
wait settle
capture sh_t20
debugview sunvis
wait settle
capture sh_t20_sunvis
debugview off

# Ground truth at the band pixel and up the column, at the last instant.
probe 800 820
probe 800 600
probe 800 400
